# RESUME_CONTRACT

What may be claimed about FlightLoop, word for word, and the evidence behind each number. Every number is rendered from `results/numbers.json` (`scripts/build_docs.py`) and checked by `scripts/check_numbers.py` (V19). If a number changes, the bullet changes with it; nobody edits this file by hand.

## Bullets

1. Built a flight-test system-identification pipeline and a blind design-iteration engine for small UAVs: on {{sysid.synth.n_seeds}} synthetic flights with turbulence and sensor noise it recovered lift and pitch derivatives within {{sysid.synth.cla_median_err_pct:.1f}}% (CLa), {{sysid.synth.cma_median_err_pct:.1f}}% (Cma) and {{sysid.synth.cmq_median_err_pct:.1f}}% (Cmq) median error, and on {{loop.blind.n_seeds}} sealed blind cases it recovered injected drag growth within {{loop.blind.max_cd0_delta_err_pp:.1f}} percentage points and static-margin shift within {{loop.blind.max_sm_delta_err_mac_pct:.2f}}% MAC; applied to {{sysid.alfa.n_flights_used}} public CMU ALFA engine-failure flights.
2. Validated SU2 low-Reynolds CFD against NASA TM-4062 wind-tunnel data with a 3-grid Celik GCI ({{e387.gci.sa.cd_fine_pct:.1f}}% on drag) and a quantified Trust Map, and trained a leave-one-family-out drag correction for XFOIL that cut drag error from {{mf.cd_mape_xfoil_pct:.1f}}% to {{mf.cd_mape_corrected_pct:.1f}}% MAPE across {{mf.n_families}} airfoil families ({{mf.n_points}} points; NeuralFoil {{mf.cd_mape_neuralfoil_pct:.1f}}%).

